# Third-party attributions

CodeStatus has no third-party runtime dependencies — `Package.swift` declares none, and the
shipped binaries link only libSystem and the Swift runtime.

It does, however, adapt small pieces of code from other MIT-licensed projects that solved the
same problems first. Those projects and the specific debts are recorded here.

---

## techgocodingnow/agentbuddy

<https://github.com/techgocodingnow/agentbuddy> — MIT License, Copyright (c) techgocodingnow.

**Adapted:** the `sockaddr_un` construction in `Sources/codestatus-hook/Transport.swift`
(`connectUnixSocket`). Filling `sun_path` from Swift requires binding a fixed-size C tuple
through `withUnsafeMutablePointer` + `withMemoryRebound`, which is easy to get subtly wrong;
their `EventSender.writeToSocket` has a correct version of it.

**Changed:** their `connect()` is blocking with no timeout, which would hang the hook — and so
delay the agent — if the daemon ever wedged. Ours is a non-blocking `connect()` followed by a
bounded `poll()`, plus `SO_SNDTIMEO` on the write.

