## bacongravy/your-turn

<https://github.com/bacongravy/your-turn> — MIT License, Copyright (c) bacongravy.

**Adapted:**

- The AppleScript automation-denied error code `-1743`, used to distinguish a denied Automation
  grant from other scripting failures so "Open session" can fall back to plain app activation
  instead of failing silently.
- The observation that `SMAppService` status `.requiresApproval` should be treated as enabled,
  so the launch-at-login toggle does not snap back while macOS waits for the user to approve it
  in System Settings.
- The idea of suppressing a notification when the frontmost terminal's *selected tab* matches
  the event's TTY — per-tab rather than per-app, so the user is not pinged about the session
  they are looking at.

